From 895d0d15497b8b07d3b7c8b08f21acb26e0e1c6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:56:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: tiles paint from the transcript cache while
 REST is in flight

An @session ref click opens a tile, and resumeTile always waited on the
latest-page REST read, so the warmed cache never reached the screen. When
REST has not landed by the time session.resume binds, the tile now publishes
the cached rows (same owner scope as the REST read) and reconciles to the
REST page when it lands, refreshing the cache. Tile opens write an
[open-timing] line tagged surface:tile, so paint:cache is observable.

Review fixes on the prefetch: unlisted sessions refetch on demand at most
every 10 min (they don't move), demand concurrency 1 on top of the tick's 2,
a throwing store read resolves 'failed' instead of escaping the IPC
listener, stale hub meta is dropped when the listing is unreadable, and the
'' -> primary host test now asserts the normalized key.
